-- title:
--   Variation of the Euler–Maclaurin correction
-- statement:
--   Let $K,N\in\mathbb N$ with $N\ge1$, $c,h\in\mathbb C$, and $r,L,a,U\in\mathbb R$.
--   Suppose $|h|\le r$, $a>0$, $a\le\operatorname{Im}c$, $a\le\operatorname{Im}(c+h)$,
--   $U\ge0$, and $|c+j|\le U$ for all $j<2K$. Then the defined correction and
--   variation bound satisfy
--   $$|\operatorname{emCorr}(K,c+h,N)-\operatorname{emCorr}(K,c,N)|
--   \le\operatorname{corrVar}(K,N,r,a,U).$$
--   The bound controls the correction throughout a cell.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/EMZetaOfflineSlab.lean#L112-L171

